Package: lxb-desktop
Version: @VERSION@-1
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: Piotr Lewandowski <piotr.petexiness@gmail.com>
Section: x11
Priority: optional
Depends: @SHLIB_DEPENDS@, lxb-compositor (= @VERSION@-1), dbus, fwupd, polkitd | policykit-1, pkexec | policykit-1,
 libwayland-client0, libwayland-egl1, libegl1, libxkbcommon0
Recommends: network-manager, wireplumber, pulseaudio-utils, hicolor-icon-theme,
 sudo, pipewire, xdg-desktop-portal
Suggests: alsa-utils, ddcutil, mesa-vulkan-drivers
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Homepage: https://github.com/Petexy/LineXinBar
Description: multi-display Wayland desktop with a console-style shell
 LineXinBar is a GPU-rendered, gamepad-friendly desktop shell. Every connected
 display is managed as an independent output.
 .
 This early-development package includes the shell, the desktop portal and a
 display-manager Wayland session. The compositor it runs on is packaged
 separately as lxb-compositor, which this package depends on.
